From: srcdynroute project <srcdynroute@local>
Subject: [PATCH 0006] srcdynroute: forced-oif takes precedence over blackhole aliases

Generated by diff -ruN against linux-6.12.111 (patches 0001-0005 already applied).
Apply with 'git apply' or 'patch -p1 -d <kbuild-root>'.

Rationale
---------
On 6.12.111 the most-specific alias wins: an `ip route add blackhole <ip>/32`
is hit in fib_table_lookup() BEFORE the output-interface filter
(fib_lookup_good_nhc()) ever runs, so a dynrt forced output interface
(flowi4_oif, set by the 0004 hooks on the reply/forward path) could not
override a more-specific blackhole.  That made the blackhole POS cases of
S4/S6/S7/S8 structurally unrescuable (0/N) and is the S5 boundary.

This makes an explicit output-interface pin beat a blackhole/unreachable/
prohibit alias: when flowi4_oif is set for the lookup, the offending
(most-specific) alias is rejected and the trie falls back to a less-specific
prefix that matches the pinned interface (the miss: -> backtrace path).  The
change is guarded by CONFIG_NF_DYNRT so it is a no-op on a vanilla kernel,
and only takes effect for lookups that actually carry a pinned oif -- i.e.
exactly the 0004 dynrt forced-oif first attempt.  During the 0004 fallback
(floweri4_oif cleared) the blackhole is honoured exactly as upstream.

Semantic note: an explicit oif pin overriding a "drop by default" blackhole
route is a defensible (and arguably more correct) interpretation, and it only
applies to lookups that already pin an output interface (dynrt here; l3mdev
/socket-bound pins elsewhere still get the pin honoured over the blackhole).

--- a/net/ipv4/fib_trie.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/fib_trie.c
@@ -1571,6 +1571,18 @@
 		fib_alias_accessed(fa);
 		err = fib_props[fa->fa_type].error;
 		if (unlikely(err < 0)) {
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NF_DYNRT)
+		/*
+		 * srcdynroute: an explicit output-interface pin set for this
+		 * lookup (flowi4_oif, by the dynrt forced-oif hook) takes
+		 * precedence over a blackhole/unreachable/prohibit alias.
+		 * Reject this (most-specific) alias and fall back to a
+		 * less-specific prefix that matches the pinned interface.
+		 * Without a pin the alias is honoured exactly as upstream.
+		 */
+		if (flp->flowi4_oif)
+			goto miss;
+#endif
 out_reject:
 #ifdef CONFIG_IP_FIB_TRIE_STATS
 			this_cpu_inc(stats->semantic_match_passed);
@@ -1584,6 +1596,11 @@
 		if (unlikely(fi->nh)) {
 			if (nexthop_is_blackhole(fi->nh)) {
 				err = fib_props[RTN_BLACKHOLE].error;
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NF_DYNRT)
+				/* srcdynroute: forced-oif also beats a blackhole nexthop */
+				if (flp->flowi4_oif)
+					goto miss;
+#endif
 				goto out_reject;
 			}

